  "_config": {
    "comment": "Concept layers — the semantic classification between entity intent and catalog filenames. resolve_entity_assets ranks layers from an entity's name/kind/model_hint tokens (kind constrains the band), then matches ONLY inside the winning layer's asset pool, so a stray shared word ('ground', 'platform') can no longer pull an unrelated asset across domains; a decisive layer with real assets yields a best-in-layer pick instead of the generic prop. Vocabulary + categories are grounded in the generated asset_catalog.json tag set (python main.py unity-catalog). 'categories' lists only UNAMBIGUOUS catalog categories for this layer (a category shared by two concepts — e.g. 'nature' holds both trees and rocks — is left out and disambiguated by keywords). 'kinds' lists entity kinds that map here (never the generic 'prop'/'object'). File missing => resolver behaves exactly as before (global match only). Deterministic: pure lookups, stable tie-breaks, no RNG, no LLM.",
    "decisive_score": 2.0,
    "kind_prior": 1.0,
    "layer_band": 0.6
  },
